<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.15;" data-page-h1>
          Automated split payouts for a marketplace
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-0" style="font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 18px); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 980px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);">
          A payment orchestration layer that automates ledgering and split payouts at the point of transaction, built for correctness, auditability, and AML aware workflows.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-7">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center heading-left mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The problem</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            A PropTech marketplace struggled with complex flow of funds. Rent payments needed to be split between Property Owners (92%), Maintenance Reserves (5%), and Platform Fees (3%) instantly.
            Manual reconciliation caused accounting errors, delayed disbursements, and potential AML compliance gaps.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-0">
            The hard part is correctness under failure: webhooks arrive out of order, retries happen, and partial outages are inevitable. Without ledger backed accounting and idempotent execution,
            duplicate charges, split errors, and reconciliation drift become unavoidable, and those mistakes are expensive when money moves across multiple stakeholders.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
          <%= render "home/case_studies/at_a_glance",
            industry: "PropTech / marketplace",
            client: "Vestra",
            country: "[[AHMAD: country]]",
            what_we_built: "Payment orchestration with double-entry ledger and automated split payouts",
            integrations: "Stripe Connect (Custom/Express), Plaid (KYC/KYB signals)",
            stack: "Next.js, NestJS, Stripe Connect" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="what-we-built">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">What we built</h2>
        <p class="large-para mb-3">
          We built a custom payment orchestration layer that automates ledgering and distribution of funds at the point of transaction, ensuring sub account accuracy and instant transparency.
        </p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          The system treats payments as stateful financial events: every charge produces ledger entries, split rules are deterministic, and payouts occur only when balances reconcile.
          Month end becomes a predictable audit step rather than a manual fire drill.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How it works</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-4" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Double entry ledgering:</strong> Database level ledger tracks virtual balances before triggering bank movements.</li>
          <li><strong>Idempotency protection:</strong> Every request is tagged with a unique key to prevent duplicate charges or split errors during timeouts.</li>
          <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> Next.js &rarr; NestJS &rarr; Stripe Connect (Custom/Express).</li>
          <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Plaid API for instant ACH verification (KYC/KYB) + Stripe for cards/wallets.</li>
          <li><strong>Security:</strong> Designed to support PCI DSS; AES 256 bank level encryption; automated SAR flagging; multi sig approvals for large withdrawals.</li>
          <li><strong>AI features:</strong> Anomaly detection monitors transaction velocity and pauses suspected account takeover (ATO) attempts.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="large-para mb-3"><strong>Ledger first correctness:</strong> Every transaction produces balanced entries before settlement; split logic is deterministic and versioned; reconciliation is a query, not a manual month end process; dispute/chargeback workflows maintain an auditable trail.</p>
        <p class="large-para mb-3"><strong>Reliability patterns:</strong> Idempotency keys across charge/split/payout operations; retry policies with backoff and dead letter handling; webhook verification and replay protection; state machines for payout lifecycle (pending &rarr; cleared &rarr; paid).</p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0"><strong>Operational readiness:</strong> Alerts on payout failures and duplicate events; runbooks for chargebacks and reconciliation audits; backfills and replay tooling for webhook driven systems; environment separation for testing money movement safely.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Results</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-0" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Zero manual reconciliation:</strong> accounting automated via real time webhooks.</li>
          <li><strong>Instant liquidity:</strong> owners receive funds via instant payouts rather than 3 to 5 day ACH waits.</li>
          <li><strong>Compliance ready:</strong> automated tax reporting and 1099 K generation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "home/case_studies/gallery", slug: "vestra-payments" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/client_quote", slug: "vestra-payments" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/cta", blurb: "We&rsquo;ll design your ledger + settlement flows for correctness, auditability, and reliability under real payment failures." %>

  <section class="py-4 bg-white">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <%= link_to "Financial services software →", industry_financial_path, class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>